{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you all for your thorough reviews. Let me summarize the four concerns that have been raised before I make my decision: First, Mr. Bell, the room capacity — the state manual limits testing rooms to 14 students maximum, so we need to split the 26 students across two rooms, 14 in Room 201 and 12 in Room 202. Second, Ms. Shah, the calculator policy — the state manual restricts calculators to section 2 only, and they must be four-function calculators, not graphing calculators. Third, Mr. Nguyen, the testing mode — the tablets cannot run the secure testing application, and the vendor has authorized paper booklets as an alternative, so we need to switch to paper-based testing. Fourth, Ms. Delgado, the storage — completed materials must be sealed in tamper-evident envelopes and stored in a locked cabinet for exactly 30 calendar days, not in the general records cabinet. I also want to address the proctor count. If we're now splitting students across two rooms, we'll need a second proctor — one per room. Before I finalize the revised plan, does anyone have any additional concerns or objections to these corrections?"}
```

